---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends stats to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink> only if you say yes when the app
      first asks. The stats cover app use, purchases, crashes, performance, app
      and device details, settings, and a random ID for each install.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your answer in the app's settings. Data already sent is
      kept with no set deletion date. It has no name or email, so your records
      cannot be found or deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck must protect the data as required by this policy and Apple's
      privacy rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      Content reports are sent by email and include game data, the sender's
      email address, and any attached drawing. They are used to review what was
      reported.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails are kept in the support inbox. To delete one, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address that sent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in {APP_NAME} tracks activity in other apps or on websites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Important changes to this policy are posted here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
